WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.091
Hi, I'm Mila.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:11.636
Today I'm excited to show you the Form
Studio 1 ecosystem

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.513
and guide you through its simple workflow.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.017
This Form Labs
SLA printer is built for a range of users,

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.603
from artists, makers and designers
to professional teams,

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:23.606
all looking for professional results
without the complexity.

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:26.776
I'll walk you through the complete
workflow, from preparing a file

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:30.363
in PreForm, to setting up your printer,
to post-processing your parts.

00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:33.825
Start to finish, this is a workflow
anyone can learn in minutes.

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:37.287
First up, let's prepare the file
you want to print.

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:42.083
Grab your design from your preferred CAD
software, model repository or 3D artist,

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.464
then open it up in PreForm – Formlabs’
free and easy print preparation software.

00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:51.342
With Formlabs’ validated print settings
for each supported material,

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.636
you can set up your
part with just one click.

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:57.932
Next, it's time to choose your layer
thickness.

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:01.519
Smaller layers give you slightly smoother
surfaces and better detail,

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.188
but they'll add to your print time.

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:07.233
For a balance between speed and detail,
I'd recommend a larger layer

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:11.196
setting like 100 microns,
but if you want a maximum fine feature

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:14.991
detail, you can drop down to something
smaller, like 30 to 50 microns.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.244
The last thing to do is select
one click print.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:22.123
It'll set up your supports,
layout and orientation automatically.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.708
All in one go.

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:25.001
Want even more control?

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:26.795
You can fine tune your setup further

00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:29.756
by making manual adjustments
to your settings.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:30.965
You can also play around

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:34.344
with advanced settings like the part
texturing and hollowing tools.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.973
Looking to use a third party resin
or adjust your print settings by hand?

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:40.100
No problem.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.853
Form Studio 1
is an open platform built for flexibility.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:49.150
Once your file is ready, you can send it
straight to your printer via Wi-Fi or USB.

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:50.944
Not near your printer?

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:54.739
Remote print’s got you covered,
letting you upload the job from anywhere.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.576
Or you can use the Formlabs
mobile app to print right from your phone

00:01:59.035 --> 00:02:02.622
Form Studio 1 comes with two resin tank
options – the Form

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:06.042
Studio 1 Resin Tank
and the Forum Studio 1 Resin Tank Pro.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.337
Check our website to confirm
material compatibility.

00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:11.923
Today
I'm printing in the Alpha White resin,

00:02:11.923 --> 00:02:14.926
so I'll use a Form Studio 1 Resin Tank.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.304
It just slides into place
and the two side latches snap shut.

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:22.976
Next, insert a Form Studio
1 build platform and latch it into place,

00:02:23.059 --> 00:02:27.689
or upgrade to the Build Platform Flex
with quick release technology to easily

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:30.692
remove parts from the build platform
without any extra tools.

00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:34.571
Last thing, insert your resin cartridge
and open the air vent.

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:38.825
Formlabs’ hassle free cartridge dispenses
resin automatically so you can switch

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:42.245
between materials without pouring
a drop of liquid resin by hand.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:46.416
Form Studio 1 will sense everything's
inserted correctly and confirm

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:48.001
that you're ready to print

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:52.046
For the safest printing workflow, add
Formlabs’ fume extraction system.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:56.676
With it in place., your Form Studio 1
ecosystem is UL Green Guard certified.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.636
Plug in the power cord.

00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:02.765
Then, on the back of your printer, remove
the fume exhaust port cover and connect

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:04.058
the hose that connects the two.

00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:08.354
Once it's powered on, you can choose
between three flow speeds.

00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:11.149
Only keep it running
for the duration of your print.

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:14.694
Once your print finishes, there are three
main steps in post-processing.

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:18.948
Rinsing in wash solvent,
removing supports, and then post curing.

00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:22.285
Formlabs
combines washing and curing into one

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:25.288
easy compact unit, the Form Wash+Cure.

00:03:25.413 --> 00:03:29.375
To wash your parts, insert the wash bucket
into the unit filled with IPA,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.545
TPM or Formlabs resin washing solution.

00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:37.217
Turn on the wash cycle for your desired
duration, letting the solvent agitate

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:41.012
around your parts to clear away
any uncured resin left over from printing.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.097
Once washing is done,

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:46.559
remove the internal basket
and using the hooks on the outside,

00:03:46.684 --> 00:03:48.728
prop it up on the edge of the wash basin

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.731
so your parts can drain
and air dry completely.

00:03:52.023 --> 00:03:55.026
Before you start curing,
make sure your parts are fully dry.

00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:58.529
We also recommend removing
any support structures before curing.

00:03:58.821 --> 00:04:01.824
Light touch supports are designed
to tear away with ease,

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:05.078
keeping support marks
to a minimum for easier finishing.

00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:08.414
Next, remove the wash bucket
and pull out the glass

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.417
turntable tucked in the back
recess of the cavity.

00:04:11.626 --> 00:04:14.420
Drop the turntable into place
at the bottom of the unit.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.006
You'll feel it slot into place
when it's seated.

00:04:17.006 --> 00:04:19.801
Place your parts on top of the turntable,
close the lid

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:22.804
and set the timer
for your desired curing duration.

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:24.722
Curing’s the last step.

00:04:24.722 --> 00:04:27.058
It’s what gives your parts
its final strength.

00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:30.353
What more of a hands off,
streamlined washing and curing experience?

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:33.481
You can always upgrade to the Form
Wash and Form Cure.

00:04:33.731 --> 00:04:34.691
And that's it.

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:35.942
Your parts are ready to go.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.652
From here, it's up to you.

00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:40.154
Sand, paint, coat or electroplate.

00:04:40.154 --> 00:04:42.573
Whatever brings your vision
to the next level.

00:04:42.573 --> 00:04:45.076
Speed, quality and accessibility.

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:48.913
The Form Studio 1 makes it easy no matter
who you are or what you're creating.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.873
Learn more and get started at formlabs.com
